 The ArrayElement type defines a type that represents the element type of a given array type T. Again, the type parameter T is constrained to be an array type using the extends keyword, and the type parameter U is used to represent the element type of the array.


 These types can be used to perform various operations on array types, such as checking whether a given type is an array type, or extracting the element type of an array type.
